  "scope": "Approved original parked sedan and waiting shelter integrated into the connected motel level, with source-preserving sparse physical/material owners, damage/supports, shared render banks and automated correctness evidence. Full vertical-slice goal remains active.",
  "changes": [
    "All 311 source solids match their supplied audit bounds; all 20,992 original triangles map to 50 sedan and 28 shelter physical/material owners. No local authoring/Python recipes run.",
    "Sedan parks at (-6,-.08,6.65), facing the guest rooms. Shelter stands at (-8,-.08,34.75), facing the connected road. Actual tire/baseplate contacts and highest existing support surface are checked. Ordinary controller navigation connects court to shelter.",
    "At most 240 cooked source triangles per contact shape retain full sparse query meshes and adjacency. Independent glazing, timber, its steel fixings and screen removal preserve other owners and real openings.",
    "One first-surviving owner submits each shared 12/3-primitive render bank. Only that leader computes the damage mask; filtered geometry updates on damage while source UVs/normals/materials/maps remain shared. Missing-art fallback draws the same physical triangles.",
    "Protocol/replay v35 records added physical objects. Older canonical map prefixes retain original IDs; malformed candidates retain explicit map boxes. Matching peers and fresh recordings are required.",
    "Production map construction services client ACKs/pings/fragments between geometry chunks. Temporary world-construction hooks are cleared before returning; optional caller-owned UI/other-transport callbacks must not touch the partial replica. Current-state publication advances transport revision without stepping gameplay.",
    "QA uses bounded dispersed port probes and services independent transports while replicas load. A forced >6.5-second constructor delay requires a reliable ping acknowledgement under unchanged six-second deadlines, with tick-zero authority/replica and cleared callbacks."
  ],
